{%- comment -%}
  Quadrant. On the OG it is 400x240, a postcard with about 144px of content
  height. On the TRMNL X the same tile is 520x390, and 390x520 in portrait, so
  it has more than twice the height. The two screens therefore hold different
  amounts, and the OG rules the cut: it shows one thing, and every row the X
  adds carries `hidden` beside its `lg:` class so the OG never sees it.

  Which one thing the OG shows depends on the weather. This plugin exists to
  carry MET's warnings (ADR-0001), so when a warning is issued the warning IS
  the OG screen and the forecast steps aside. On the X the warning is a band
  across the top and the forecast keeps its place, as on every other layout.
  The OG quadrant is the only screen anywhere that drops the forecast, because
  it is the only one with no room to do both.

  What the X adds under the hero: the next twelve hours, then the next four
  days, each behind a rule. Both bands copy the half horizontal's, so a mashup
  of the two reads as one plugin.

  The day band is the first row to go when the tile is short. Landscape is
  390px tall against portrait's 520px, and the hero plus the hours already fill
  it, so the day band is hidden again there. `lg:portrait:` is what puts it
  back.

  The hour temperature is the one size that has to change with the orientation.
  Six columns of 520px give 87px each, which `value--base` fits; six columns of
  390px give 65px, where it collides with its neighbour. Portrait drops it to
  `value--small`.

  No title bar was the earlier cut: #9 puts the CC BY credit on the full screen
  and both halves, and leaves the quadrant to carry it in the author bio. The
  bar came back in a9c0e89, so the credit line here stays short.

  A failed warnings poll still shows the conditions, with the marker #19 asked
  for. Silence here would read as "no warnings" on the very screen whose job is
  to show them.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- comment -%} The forecast hides only where the warning has taken its place,
     which is the OG and nothing else. {%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign forecast_show = "flex" -%}
{%- if warn_count > 0 -%}{%- assign forecast_show = "hidden lg:flex" -%}{%- endif -%}

{% if forecast_ok == false and warn_count == 0 %}

  <div class="layout layout--col layout--center gap--small">
    <span class="value value--small">No forecast data</span>
    <span class="label label--small">MET Norway did not answer</span>
  </div>

{% else %}

  <div class="layout layout--col layout--center gap--small">

    {% if warn_count > 0 %}

      {%- comment -%} The OG: the warning is the postcard. {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="flex flex--col flex--center-x flex--center-y gap--small lg:hidden">
        <div class="flex flex--row flex--center-y gap--small bg--black px--2 py--1">
          <span class="title title--small text--white">&#9888; {{ warn_level }}</span>
        </div>
        <span class="title title--base text--center" data-clamp="2">{{ warn_event }}</span>
        <span class="label label--small text--center" data-clamp="1">
          {{ warn_area }}{% if warn_count > 1 %} &middot; +{{ warn_count | minus: 1 }} more{% endif %}
        </span>
      </div>

      {%- comment -%} The X: the warning is a band, and the forecast stays. The
           area name goes, as on both halves: the band has one line. {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="hidden lg:flex flex--row flex--center-y gap--small bg--black px--2">
        <span class="label label--small text--white">&#9888; {{ warn_level }}</span>
        <span class="label label--small text--white" data-clamp="1">{{ warn_event }}</span>
        {% if warn_count > 1 %}
          <div class="grow"></div>
          <span class="label label--small text--white">+{{ warn_count | minus: 1 }}</span>
        {% endif %}
      </div>

    {% endif %}

    {% if forecast_ok %}

      <div class="{{ forecast_show }} flex--col flex--center-x flex--center-y gap--small w--full">

        {%- comment -%} Now. {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="flex flex--col flex--center-x gap--none">
          <div class="flex flex--row flex--center-y gap">
            {% render "weather_icon", code: now_symbol, box: "w--[56px] h--[56px] lg:w--[88px] lg:h--[88px]" %}
            <span class="value value--xlarge lg:value--xxlarge value--tnums" data-fit-value="true">{{ now_temp | round: 0 }}&deg;</span>
          </div>
          <span class="label label--small text--center" data-clamp="1">
            Feels {{ now_feels | round: 0 }}&deg; &middot; {{ now_wind | round: 0 }} m/s {{ now_dir }}
          </span>
        </div>

        {%- comment -%} The X only: the next twelve hours. {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="divider divider--h hidden lg:block"></div>
        <div class="hidden lg:grid grid--cols-6">
          {% for record in hour_list %}
            {% assign hour = record | split: "|" %}
            <div class="flex flex--col flex--center-x gap--none">
              <span class="label label--small">{{ hour[0] | times: 1 | date: "%H" }}</span>
              {% render "weather_icon", code: hour[2], box: "w--[52px] h--[52px]" %}
              <span class="value value--base lg:portrait:value--small value--tnums">{{ hour[1] }}&deg;</span>
              <span class="label label--small">{% if hour[3] %}{{ hour[3] }}{{ hour[4] }}{% else %}&nbsp;{% endif %}</span>
            </div>
          {% endfor %}
        </div>

        {%- comment -%} The X in portrait only: the next four days. {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="divider divider--h hidden lg:portrait:block"></div>
        <div class="hidden lg:portrait:grid grid--cols-4">
          {% for record in day_list limit: 4 %}
            {% assign day = record | split: "|" %}
            <div class="flex flex--col flex--center-x gap--none">
              <span class="label label--small">{% if forloop.first %}Today{% else %}{{ day[0] | times: 1 | date: "%a" }}{% endif %}</span>
              {% render "weather_icon", code: day[3], box: "w--[52px] h--[52px]" %}
              <span class="value value--base value--tnums">{{ day[1] | round: 0 }}&deg;</span>
              <span class="label label--small">{{ day[2] | round: 0 }}&deg;</span>
            </div>
          {% endfor %}
        </div>

      </div>

    {% else %}

      {%- comment -%} A warning with no forecast behind it. The OG is showing the
           warning and has no room to say more; the X has the space. {%- endcomment -%}
      <span class="hidden lg:block label label--small">No forecast data</span>

    {% endif %}

    {% if warnings_ok == false %}
      <span class="label label--small label--outline">Warnings unavailable</span>
    {% endif %}

  </div>

{% endif %}

<div class="title_bar">
  <img class="image image-stroke" src="data:image/svg+xml;base64,{{ svg_logo | base64_encode }}" />
  <span class="title">{{ place | default: "Forecast" }}</span>
  <span class="instance">MET Norway</span>
</div>
